I can't think of any monsters for whom it would be a good idea to do
so -- most are undead, and bad to eat for other reasons.

If it's a ring that grants death resistance, the user might be able to
gain it permanently by eating the ring.  But that might be too
powerful.  I like the idea of forcing the user to have to expend one
of his limited number of equipment slots to remain protected from
death effects.  It's just that currently the slot that must be devoted
to that most be either the Cloak slot (when there are cloaks of
Protection, Invisibility and Displacement that would also be great in
that position) and/or the primary armor slot (which is often taken up
by Gray Dragon Scale Mail by the time the player enters Gehennom).

There are two ring slots however, so if the player uses one to gain
death resistance, it works as a nice trade-off against using a
different, unique slot for magic resistance, which is still more
useful.

I'd say the question to ask is: is a Ring Versus Death plus a Cloak of
Displacement roughly as useful as (in different ways) to a Cloak of
Magic Resistance?

The problem with the trade-off is that without Magic Resistance,
you're still vulnerable to Destroy Armor spells.

